SUMMARY:Community Engagement Forum with The Mama Joe Project
DESCRIPTION:The Mama Joe Project centers storytelling via documentary film for educational outreach on aging\, caregiving\, and dementia. This is a free event\, open to all ages and audiences in and near The Triangle. We incorporate a screening of the documentary film “My Mama Joe\, Hope & Help” with a min-info fair featuring local resource vendors\, and a Q&A session with area subject matter experts. The goal is to better connect attendees with information\, resources\, and social networks to improve health and quality of life
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/community-engagement-forum-with-the-mama-joe-project/
LOCATION:PSI Theatre at Durham Arts Council\, 120 Morris Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
